      "description": "Watch Wolverhampton vs Port Vale highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 7, 2026. The Carabao Cup atmosphere was electric as Wolverhampton Wanderers hosted Port Vale on 2026-08-07 . Both sides took to the pitch with high hopes of progressing in this early-season knockout clash, setting the stage for a compelling encounter. First Half Dominance Wolverhampton Wanderers wasted little time establishing their authority. After an early scare for the visitors when Marshall Munetsi ’s effort was saved, Adam Armstrong broke the deadlock in the 14th minute. The forward clinical finish into the bottom right corner gave the hosts a well-deserved lead. Armstrong almost doubled his tally shortly after, but his long-range strike rattled the right post, keeping the scoreline thin for a brief moment. However, the pressure from the home side was relentless. In the 34th minute, André found the net from close range with a header, expertly assisted by Yerson Mosquera following a corner. The game was effectively put beyond doubt just before the break when Fer López converted a left-footed shot from the center of the box in the 43rd minute, thanks to a sharp setup by Rodrigo Gomes . Penalty Drama and Solid Defense The second half offered Port Vale a lifeline when Mo Faal drew a foul from Mosquera in the box at the 54-minute mark. However, the resulting penalty was brilliantly saved by Dan Bentley , who stood tall to deny Faal ’s central effort. That moment seemed to deflate the visitors' hopes of a comeback as the hosts began to manage the clock and introduce fresh legs. Substitutions followed, with Raúl Jiménez and Tommy Doyle entering the fray for the Wolverhampton Wanderers . While Port Vale ’s Oliver Lynch and Ben Waine attempted late efforts to salvage pride, Bentley and the defensive line remained resolute. The match concluded with a professional display from the top-flight side, securing a clean sheet and a convincing victory to advance in the Carabao Cup ."
