      "description": "Watch Millwall vs Newcastle highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 8, 2026. The Carabao Cup took center stage on September 8, 2026, as Millwall hosted Newcastle United in a match filled with tactical intrigue. Both sides entered the pitch looking to assert their dominance and secure progress in the competition under the floodlights. Stalemate in the First Stanza Newcastle United started with intent, dominating possession and pinning the hosts back. Jacob Murphy and Harvey Barnes were active early on, firing shots that tested the defensive resolve of the home side. However, Millwall remained dangerous on the break, and Lyndon Dykes forced a brilliant save from Lukás Hornícek in the 26th minute with a shot aimed at the top corner. Caleb Taylor also proved to be a handful in the air, narrowly missing with two headers from set-pieces as the first half ended goalless. Willock Finds the Breakthrough As the second half progressed, the pressure from the Magpies intensified. Filip Marschall was kept busy in the Millwall goal, denying Joe Willock and Harvey Barnes with a series of sharp saves. The game reached a boiling point in the 79th minute when Taïryk Arconte broke free for the hosts, only to see his right-footed effort crash against the post. It was a massive let-off for the Premier League side, and they capitalized on that momentum shift almost immediately. In the 81st minute, the deadlock was finally broken. Lewis Hall delivered a pinpoint cross into the box, finding Joe Willock , who clinicaly slotted a left-footed shot into the bottom right corner. Despite a late flurry of substitutions and a yellow card for Alfie Massey during stoppage time, Newcastle United managed to see out the game and secure their place in the next round of the sports calendar's most unpredictable cup."
